---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
const recipes = [
  { slug: "landing", title: "Business landing", text: "Hero, benefits, example pricing, FAQ and footer. Uses container, grid, cards, buttons, disclosure and dialog." },
  { slug: "catalog", title: "Editorial catalogue", text: "Card grid with simple filters and a detail view. Labelled placeholder covers, breadcrumb, badges, pagination and tabs." },
  { slug: "admin", title: "Admin panel", text: "Sidebar drawer, forms, a responsive table, alerts, progress and toasts. Fictional data, no backend." },
];
---
<Base title="Examples" description="Three complete recipes built only with iVOLT: a business landing page, an editorial catalogue and a static admin panel. Open them or copy the folders.">
  <article class="docs-prose">
    <h1>Examples</h1>
    <p>Three complete pages that share the framework but not the composition. Each recipe is a standalone HTML file that links the prebuilt assets from a sibling <code>ivolt/</code> folder, exactly like the plain HTML starter. Data and forms are demos: nothing is sent anywhere.</p>
    <div class="iv-grid iv-u-gap-4 iv-u-grid-cols-1 iv-u-md-grid-cols-3" style="max-inline-size: none">
      {recipes.map((r) => (
        <article class="iv-card">
          <div class="iv-card__body"><h2 class="iv-card__title">{r.title}</h2><p class="iv-u-m-0">{r.text}</p></div>
          <div class="iv-card__footer"><a class="iv-button iv-button--primary iv-button--sm" href={`/examples/${r.slug}/index.html`}>Open</a></div>
        </article>
      ))}
    </div>
    <h2>Copy a recipe</h2>
    <p>Each recipe lives in <code>examples/recipes/&lt;name&gt;/index.html</code> in the repository. Copy that folder together with <code>examples/recipes/ivolt/</code> (created by <code>node scripts/sync-examples.mjs</code> after a build) and open the page. The plain starter in <code>examples/plain-html</code> is the smallest possible version of the same setup.</p>
  </article>
</Base>
